-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles Hecke module free over 𝒪[Δ_Q]
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and $p$ a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ trivial on some finite subextension) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ has no proper nonzero stable subspace. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals with $p\in S$, let $N\ge 1$ have all its prime factors in $S$, and let $r\ge 5$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $p\nmid r-1$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ with $\ell\notin S$ and the $U_q$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, one has $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ in $k[X]$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct primes, none in $S$, none equal to $r$, each equal to $1$ in $k$, and let $\alpha_i\in k$ satisfy $\alpha_i^2-\theta(T_{q_i})\alpha_i+q_i=0$ and $2\alpha_i\neq\theta(T_{q_i})$ (a simple root). Let $\pi^\Delta_i:(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to \mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)})$ be surjective homomorphisms, write $L=N(\prod_i q_i)r$, $\Delta_Q=\prod_i \mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)})$, let $\pi_Q:(\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to\Delta_Q$ be the product of the $\pi^\Delta_i$ composed with reduction, $H_R=\ker((\mathbb Z/L)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/r)^\times)$ and $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker\pi_Q$. Assume a non-Eisenstein condition: some prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ and $\ell\equiv 1 \pmod L$ has $\theta(T_\ell)\neq \ell+1$. Finally assume `hc`, that the auxiliary-level operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\neq r$) commute on the carrier $H^1(N r,\ \mathrm{subgroup}\,N\,r;\mathcal O)$; write $M_{Nr}$ for the associated localisation $\mathrm{ML}$ of that carrier at the complement of the kernel of the map $\mathcal O[X_g]\to k$ sending $X_{T_\ell}\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$, and $d=\mathrm{finrank}_{\mathcal O}M_{Nr}$. Then there exist: a proof `hcQ` that the level-$L$ operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$) and $U_{q_i}$ commute on $H^1(L,H_Q;\mathcal O)$; a proof `hdc` that all diamond operators of $(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ commute with those operators; and an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $D:\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]\to\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(M_Q)$, where $M_Q$ is the corresponding localisation of $H^1(L,H_Q;\mathcal O)$ at the complement of the kernel of $X_{T_\ell}\mapsto\theta(T_\ell)$, $X_{U_{q_i}}\mapsto\alpha_i$, such that: $D$ sends the group element $\pi_Q(u)$ to the diamond operator `diaML` of $u$ for every $u\in H_R$; every $\delta\in\Delta_Q$ is $\pi_Q(u)$ for some $u\in H_R$; $M_Q$ is a finite $\mathcal O$-module; there is a family $b_1,\dots,b_d$ in $M_Q$ which is a basis of $M_Q$ for the $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$-action through $D$, that is every $x\in M_Q$ is $\sum_i D(c_i)(b_i)$ for some $c_i\in\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$, and $\sum_i D(c_i)(b_i)=0$ holds exactly when all $c_i=0$; and there is a surjective $\mathcal O$-linear map $\mathrm{lam}:M_Q\to M_{Nr}$ which intertwines the action of $X_{T_\ell}$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$ with the action of the corresponding auxiliary-level generator, satisfies $\mathrm{lam}\circ \mathrm{diaML}(u)=\mathrm{lam}$ for all $u\in H_R$, and has kernel exactly the $\mathcal O$-span of the elements $D(\delta)z-z$ with $\delta\in\Delta_Q$, $z\in M_Q$.
--
--   This is the Hecke-module half of the Taylor–Wiles construction at a set $Q=\{q_1,\dots,q_t\}$ of Taylor–Wiles primes: the localised cohomology module at level $L=N(\prod q_i)r$ with group $H_Q$ is free of rank $d$ over $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$, and its coinvariants for $\Delta_Q$ are identified Hecke-equivariantly with the auxiliary level-$Nr$ module. It is used to produce the Taylor–Wiles modules carrying the $p$-adic Galois representations in the patching argument.
